"n1":{"x":2880,"y":0,"w":400,"fill":"green","size":"m","text":"Screens are drawn at the real 320×240 px and shown at 2×.\n\nCorner = knob: each tile sits in the corner of the screen nearest its knob (K1 top-left, K2 top-right, K3 bottom-left, K4 bottom-right, as in hardware §8.2).\n\n'Melon Drive' and the preset names are placeholders."},
"n2":{"x":2880,"y":900,"w":400,"fill":"blue","size":"m","text":"Every list works the same way:\nK1 turn = move\nK1 push = back\nK4 push = open / load\nK2 turn = bank (presets)\n\nFootswitch tap still toggles bypass on every screen."},
"n3":{"x":2880,"y":1800,"w":400,"fill":"orange","size":"m","text":"Stage-critical info (preset name, BYPASS, tuner note, value pop-up) is ≥24 px, about 3 mm or more on the 2\" panel, so it can be read standing.\n\nSmall 12 px text is only for things you read while bent over the pedal."}
